9479	{"artifactId":"LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s4","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s4-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-20T07:30:14.247Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers S004's section grouping, neighbour summaries and single-result acceptance criteria.","evidence":"DEF §6.4 requires coherent section chunks (ac1), summaries across chunk boundaries (ac2), and one result using today's verdict rules (ac3). The proposed material builder, neighbourSummary and merge/finish address these three requirements. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/DEF.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"HLD/LLD use one template reviewer session; other stages extract claims and verify each claim separately.","evidence":"runReview dispatches through `if (isDesignStage(opts.stage)) return runTemplateReview(...)`; otherwise it calls extractClaims, gatherEvidence and a serial verifyOrRecord loop. runTemplateReview sends the whole document and permits one correction after invalid output. HARD_REVIEW_DEADLINE_MS is 30 minutes. [files: src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/workflow/review/template.ts, src/workflow/review/extract.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"buildBatchedVerifyPrompt is private to claims.ts, has the stated signature, and has only handleClaims as its caller.","evidence":"Repository search found its declaration and sole invocation in claims.ts. Its body accepts readonly Claim[] and Evidence[], builds an evidence map by claimId, and returns `{ system, user }` using buildVerifyPrompt and renderEvidence. [files: src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/claims.ts, src/workflow/review/verify.ts]","action":"Move the helper and update the import as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A new parsed answer representation is needed to retain file sets and notApplicable reasons before merging.","evidence":"validateTemplateAnswer currently converts directly to Finding[]. It omits notApplicable items and embeds files into evidence using `[files: ...]`; Finding has no files field. Searches found no existing parseTemplateAnswer implementation. [files: src/workflow/review/template.ts, src/workflow/review/types.ts]","action":"Preserve the existing validation and finding conversion semantics in the new parser.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Using the heading-path slug as an atom ID is sufficient to identify every section independently.","evidence":"S004 specifies `id = the heading path slug`, without collision handling. HLD sc3 represents chunk membership as `atomIds: readonly string[]`, and sc1 references endpoints only through `from` and `to`. Two sibling sections with identical headings therefore receive the same identity, making membership and reference resolution ambiguous and potentially reviewing the wrong section. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S004/LLD.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md]","action":"Assign deterministic occurrence-qualified atom IDs, separate them from anchor slugs, and test repeated headings and slug collisions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Prefixing a raw claim ID with its chunk makes every raw claim ID job-unique.","evidence":"normalizeClaims preserves every supplied nonempty ID: `const id = typeof c.id === 'string' && c.id.length > 0 ? c.id : ...`; it performs no uniqueness check. Two distinct claims with local ID c1 in the same chunk both become `c<chunk>-c1`. S004 explicitly promises distinct raw IDs for this case, but its formula produces colliding source identifiers and ambiguous provenance. [files: src/workflow/review/extract.ts, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Include the claim's occurrence index in rawId, retaining the model's local ID separately. Test duplicate IDs within one chunk as well as across chunks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S001 already provides the multi-answer snapshot commit behavior required by the divided extraction stage.","evidence":"S001 §2.17 says claims are saved 'the moment the extract stage's answer is applied' and written once. S004 requires accumulating multiple answers and committing only after the last. No review-pipeline implementation was found to establish how stage completion, aggregation and snapshot writes interact. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S001/LLD.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Make S001's stage-completion contract explicitly cover multiple extraction answers and the merged claim/evidence output, then verify resume between answers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Returning multiple relation prompts and using semantic validation and neighbour summaries are supported S001 contract extensions.","evidence":"Although HLD sc2 sketches a single relation prompt, S001 §2.22 explicitly refines it to `readonly ChunkPrompt[]`. Sections 2.19 and 2.21 also define optional AdapterStage.validate and ReviewAdapter.neighbourSummary. S004 consumes these owner-defined extensions. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S001/LLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A premise that fails verification twice is retained as MED not judged and blocks under the default policy.","evidence":"verifyOrRecord makes two attempts, propagates AbortError, and then returns severity MED with evidence beginning `Not judged`. DEFAULT_BLOCK_ON is ['HIGH', 'MED']. verifyClaim passes VERIFY_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS = 180000. Existing tests assert that other findings survive and the resulting verdict blocks. [files: src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/verify.ts, src/workflow/review/verdict.ts, src/workflow/review/__tests__/review.test.ts]","action":"Preserve these behaviors through the pipeline failure policy.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Invalid checklist answers are detectable with existing validation and fail the review after one corrective retry.","evidence":"validateTemplateAnswer rejects missing, repeated or unknown items, excess premises, and does-not-hold premises without files. runTemplateReview adds correction text, retries once, and throws `No review was recorded` after a second invalid answer. [files: src/workflow/review/template.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts]","action":"Keep relation-answer validation distinct from full-checklist validation when relation calls return only selected items.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream S004 acceptance criterion maps to a proposed test.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.4 with the supplied acceptance mapping: ac1 maps to whole-section splitting and coherent chunk integration tests; ac2 to reference-summary tests; ac3 to divided template/premise report and verdict tests. Existing template and premise tests provide concrete validation, severity and retry expectations. This verifies test-plan coverage, not execution of the proposed tests. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/DEF.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S004/LLD.md, src/workflow/review/__tests__/template.test.ts, src/workflow/review/__tests__/review.test.ts]","action":"Add the atom-ID and raw-claim-ID collision cases identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-20T07:30:14.247Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
